{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"hinze-2018-on","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"On constructing 2-3 trees"}]},"title_text":"On constructing 2-3 trees","kind":"reference","taxon":null,"url":"hinze-2018-on.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"reference","attrs":[["entry","hinze-2018-on"],["kind","reference"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"abstract","attrs":[],"body":{"Inline":[{"Text":"We consider the task of constructing 2-3 trees. Given a sequence of elements we seek to build a 2-3 tree–in linear time–that contains the elements in symmetric order. We discuss three approaches: top-down, bottom-up, and incremental. The incremental approach is more flexible than the other two in that it allows us to interleave the construction work with other operations, for example, queries."}]}}},{"Group":{"role":"entry-links","attrs":[],"body":{"Inline":[{"Span":{"role":"entry-link","attrs":[["field","pdf-url"]],"body":[{"Link":{"url":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/129759AE03543B461536F78B386D93B5/S0956796818000187a.pdf/div-class-title-on-constructing-2-3-trees-div.pdf","body":[{"Text":"PDF"}]}}]}},{"Text":" · "},{"Span":{"role":"entry-link","attrs":[["field","doi"]],"body":[{"Link":{"url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/s0956796818000187","body":[{"Text":"DOI"}]}}]}},{"Text":" · "},{"Span":{"role":"entry-link","attrs":[["field","pldb"]],"body":[{"Link":{"url":"https://pldb.kirancodes.me/p/journals/jfp/Hinze18","body":[{"Text":"pldb"}]}}]}}]}}}]}}}]}}
